      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "UNLABELLED",
          "content": "The hemodynamic effect of mepindolol-sulfate, a new non-cardioselective beta-receptor blocking agent, was compared with the hemodynamic effect of propranolol at rest and during exercise in five patients with coronary artery disease during an eight week double blind cross-over study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "1. The beta-receptor blocking effect of mepindolol-sulfate is 25 times higher than that of propranolol. 2. No hemodynamic difference between mepindolol-sulfate and propranolol was seen at rest. 3. The increase of blood pressure during exercise was less pronounced during mepindolol-sulfate-medication compared to propranolol. 4. Propranolol seems to achieve a more pronounced negative inotropic effect than mepindolol-sulfate."
        }
      ]},
